#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:2
msgid "Localization and Internationalization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:4
msgid ""
"In this article, we explain high-level approaches to internationalizing "
"and localizing your documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:6
msgid ""
"By default, Read the Docs assumes that your documentation is or *might "
"become* multilingual one day. The initial default language is English and"
" therefore you often see the initial build of your documentation "
"published at ``/en/latest/``, where the ``/en`` denotes that it's in "
"English. By having the ``en`` URL component present from the beginning, "
"you are ready for the eventuality that you would want a second language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:13
msgid ""
"Read the Docs supports hosting your documentation in multiple languages. "
"Read below for the various approaches that we support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:20
msgid "Projects with one language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:22
msgid ""
"If your documentation isn't in English (the default), you should indicate"
" which language you have written it in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:25
msgid ""
"It is easy to set the language of your project. In your project's "
":menuselection:`Settings` (or when adding the project), simply select "
"your desired :guilabel:`Language` from the dropdown. This will tell Read "
"the Docs that your project is in the language. The language will be "
"represented in the URL for your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:31
msgid ""
"For example, a project that is in Spanish will have a default URL of "
"``/es/latest/`` instead of ``/en/latest/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:35
msgid "Projects with multiple translations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:39
msgid ":doc:`guides/manage-translations-sphinx`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:40
msgid ""
"Describes the whole process for a Sphinx documentation projects with "
"multiples languages in the same repository and how to keep the "
"translations updated on time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:43
msgid ""
"Each language must have its own project on Read the Docs. You will choose"
" one to be the parent project, and add each of the other projects as "
"\"Translations\" of the parent project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:47
msgid "Let's use ``godot`` as an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:49
msgid ""
"The ``godot`` project is the parent. Each translation then has its own "
"project, for example ``godot-es``. The *Language* for ``godot-es`` is set"
" to ``Spanish``. Then, on the  *Translations* page of the ``godot`` "
"project, ``godot-es`` is set as translation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:54
msgid "This has the results of serving:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:56
msgid "``godot`` at ``https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:57
msgid "``godot-es`` at ``https://docs.godotengine.org/es/stable/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:59
msgid "It also gets included in the Read the Docs :term:`flyout menu`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:64
msgid ""
"The default language of a custom domain is determined by the language of "
"the parent project that the domain was configured on. See :doc:`/custom-"
"domains` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:70
msgid "Translation workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:72
msgid ""
"When you work with translations, the workflow of your translators becomes"
" a critical component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:75
msgid "Considerations include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:77
msgid ""
"Are your translators able to use a Git workflow? For instance, are they "
"able to translate directly via GitHub?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:78
msgid "Do you benefit from machine translation?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:79
msgid ""
"Do you need different roles, for instance do you need translators and "
"editors?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:80
msgid "What is your source language?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/localization.rst:81
msgid "When are your translated versions published?"
msgstr ""

